## 7. Web & Android Security Analysis

### Web Client Security:
* **XSS Resistance:** The UI is constructed in React 19. All user inputs (task names, notes, custom subjects) are escaped automatically via JSX virtual DOM binding.
* **Calendar Drag Sanitization:** Inspected [`src/components/StudyCalendar.tsx`](file:///c:/Users/pc/Downloads/levelup-study%20(5)/src/components/StudyCalendar.tsx) for innerHTML usage; found only safe date numeric primitives.
* **HTTP Security Headers:**
  - `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff` (prevents MIME-confusion attacks)
  - `X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN` (mitigates clickjacking)
  - `Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin` (prevents path leakage in referrer)
  - `Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload` (enforces HTTPS)
  - `Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()` (disables unused hardware APIs)

### Android Mobile Security (OWASP MASVS):
* **Cleartext Traffic Prohibition (MASVS-NETWORK-1):** Enforced via [`network_security_config.xml`](file:///c:/Users/pc/Downloads/levelup-study%20(5)/android/app/src/main/res/xml/network_security_config.xml):
